{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e226f806-1397-4825-8249-06aa5234b29a","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Find the area enclosed by these curves. First, locate their intersections to determine the integration limits.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Area between two curves"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.1,1.15],"y":[-0.1,1.2],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"upper","y":"x","domain":[0,1.08],"label":"y = x"},{"kind":"fn","id":"lower","y":"x^2","domain":[0,1.08],"label":"y = x²"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"intersections","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x=x^2\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad x(x-1)=0"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e226f806-1397-4825-8249-06aa5234b29a","step":{"id":"s2","script":"The curves meet at zero and one. Between them, the line is above the parabola, so each vertical strip has height x minus x squared.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"strip","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"start","at":{"on":"upper","x":0},"label":"(0, 0)"},{"kind":"point","id":"end","at":{"on":"upper","x":1},"label":"(1, 1)"},{"kind":"segment","id":"height","from":{"on":"lower","x":0.5},"to":{"on":"upper","x":0.5},"stroke":"dashed","label":"height"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"height_eq","anchor":{"el":"intersections","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"h(x)=y_{\\text{top}}-y_{\\text{bottom}}=x-x^2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Which expression gives the strip height: x − x² or x² − x? Why?","expected_gist":"x − x², because the line is above the parabola on the interval from zero to one."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e226f806-1397-4825-8249-06aa5234b29a","step":{"id":"s3","script":"Adding all those thin strips gives the shaded area: integrate top minus bottom from the left intersection to the right intersection.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"shading","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"shade","id":"enclosed","between":["upper","lower"],"from":0,"to":1}]},{"op":"equation","id":"integral","anchor":{"el":"height_eq","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\int_0^1(x-x^2)\\,dx=\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}-\\frac{x^3}{3}\\right]_0^1"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"e226f806-1397-4825-8249-06aa5234b29a","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Evaluating at the endpoints gives one sixth of a square unit. Always check which curve is on top before subtracting.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"integral","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A=\\frac12-\\frac13=\\boxed{\\frac16}\\ \\text{square units}"},{"op":"figure","id":"area_label","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[0.72,0.61],"text":"A = 1/6","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
